    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0898" n="1856" xml:id="pg1856"/>

                <head>No. 36.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lothrop to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-22"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 22, 1888</date>.
                        (Received March 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 161.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch, No. 110, relative to the
                    protection of fur-bearing seals in the Behring Sea, has just reached me, and I
                    have lost no time in making known to the imperial Government your wishes
                    respecting the co-operation of the Russian ambassador in London with Mr. Phelps
                    on this subject.</p>
                <p>Very truly, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. V. N.
                    Lothrop.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
